<section><h2>AI handoff archive retention</h2><p>New copies: 60 per IP address per hour and 1,000 site-wide per hour. Maximum 100 MiB of new archive text per UTC day and 4 MiB per copy; oversized contexts are rejected, never truncated. Archived reads remain available.</p><p>Cleanup removes only unused copies older than 30 days. Every archive linked to a submitted packet is retained, including quarantined and rejected packets, until explicit research deletion.</p><p>Stored archives: <?=e(one('SELECT COUNT(*) n FROM workflow_handoffs')['n'])?> · Last cleanup (UTC): <?=e(setting('handoff_cleanup_at','Not run'))?> · Removed in last run: <?=e(setting('handoff_cleanup_deleted','0'))?></p><form method="post"><?=csrf()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="handoffs"><button>Clean up expired unused handoffs</button></form><p class="fine">Schedule daily: php bin/console.php handoffs-prune. Each run handles up to 100 research projects; repeat for a backlog. Keep a private backup before maintenance.</p></section>
<section><h2>Private database backups</h2><p>Create a consistent SQL export in private storage. It includes confidential records and must never be served publicly. Downloading secrets through this interface is intentionally unavailable. Back up uploaded files and environment configuration separately.</p><p>Last successful export: <?=e(setting('backup_last_at','Not yet created'))?> · <?=e(setting('backup_last_bytes','0'))?> bytes</p><form method="post"><?=csrf()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="backup"><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_backup" value="yes" required> I understand this creates a sensitive backup in private server storage.</label><button>Create private database backup</button></form><p class="fine">The operator can retrieve files from storage/backups using private hosting access. CLI alternative: php bin/console.php backup. Verify restoration before launch.</p></section>